From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SheepyLord <37598021+SheepyLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 05:12:08 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Never save over unread settings, retry saves and keep links

A config file that does not exist now reads as a complete, empty file, so
Discard Changes and Revert All Unsaved Changes discard edits on a fresh
profile without user.conf (or rtx.conf) instead of refusing and keeping
them (regression from the atomic-save patch).

A file that exists but cannot be read when its option layer or LocalData
scope is created (held by a sync or backup tool, a read error) no longer
becomes an empty layer that a Save would write over: Save and export of
that layer, and saving the diagnostic choices, refuse until a reload
reads it; the diagnostic policy then leaves the SDK database alone and
reporting stays off. An export target that cannot be read is not
replaced either. The log and both menus say so.

Saves retry for up to half a second while another process briefly holds
the file, rewrite the target of a symbolic link or a hard-linked file in
place (the staged copy is kept if that write fails midway) instead of
replacing the name, and a failed save is shown: Save Settings turns red
with the reason in its tooltip, and the developer menu's layer buttons
show it in red text.

rtx.gmod.ignoreOutlineMeshes no longer hides view-model draws (flipped
view models and their hands), mirrored geometry (a negative determinant
in the object or bone transform) or replacement meshes that set their
own culling; RtxModelLayers::isIgnoredOutline holds the rule.

Two new messages are translated in all six catalogs. RtxOptions.md gains
the rtx.gmod.importedModelSmoothNormalTextures entry its patch left out,
so test_documentation passes again.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
